# GCPM water: LAMMPS deck set up to mirror the reference Fortran run
#
# The reference run is the GCPM Fortran code in MD_water/MD_water, driven by
# its control file pwat1.dat and its parameter file param.  Every setting below
# that has a Fortran counterpart is taken from those two files:
#
#  Fortran (pwat1.dat / param / hard-coded)   LAMMPS here
#  ----------------------------------------   ---------------------------------
#  NC = 5  -> 4*NC^3 = 500 molecules          data.gcpm5 (500 mols, 2500 sites)
#  rho = 0.997 g/cm3 -> L = 24.6553681 Ang    box of data.gcpm5, replicate 1
#  T = 298.15 K                               variable T
#  reduced dt 6e-4 -> 0.98213053 fs           timestep
#      (dt = 6e-4 * sigma * sqrt(m/eps),
#       m = 2*mh+mo = 17.99743 amu)
#  1000000 steps -> 982.13 ps                 variable nsteps (short by default)
#  RCUT = 10 sigma, capped at Lmin - skin     variable rc = 11.220684
#      -> 11.220684 Ang
#  skin = 0.3 sigma = 1.107 Ang               neighbor 1.107 bin
#  KSORT = 10 (list rebuild interval)         neigh_modify (distance check, see below)
#  dielectric = 78.4 (hard-coded in           pair_style gcpm 1 78.4 ...
#      diel_cerf_hbond.f, overriding the
#      T,rho correlation above it)
#  tol_dipole = 1e-8, maxiter = 10            polar/tol 1.8e-5, polar/maxiter 50
#      (crit = max component of (dmu)^2 in        (1e-4 reduced dipole units per
#       reduced units, so 1e-4 per component)      component = 1.82e-5 e*Ang;
#                                                  the LAMMPS solver needs 10-12
#                                                  iterations for that, so the
#                                                  Fortran cap of 10 is left off
#                                                  and the tolerance is actually
#                                                  reached every step)
#  Evans Gaussian isokinetic thermostat       fix rigid/nvk/small (one friction
#      (Pos_alc.f alpha1, one alpha over          over translation + rotation,
#       translation + rotation)                   same constraint)
#  rescale to T every 4000 steps              not needed: nvk holds the kinetic
#      (pre_corrc_average.f)                      energy fixed to begin with
#  mo = 2.6564834e-23 g, mh = 1.6603021e-24 g set type ... mass (see below)
#  epsilon = 110 K = 0.218445 kcal/mol,       pair_coeff lines
#      sigma = 3.69 Ang, gamma(buck) = 12.75,
#      Gaussian widths 0.610 (O/M) and
#      0.455 (H), polarizability 1.444 Ang^3
#  gofr.dat: 334 bins of 0.0369 Ang,          compute rdf (same bins, same
#      sampled every KSORT steps, all             sampling interval, intra-
#      intermolecular site pairs                  molecular pairs excluded)
#  meansq.dat: COM mean squared displacement  compute msd on the O sites
#      every 200 steps                            (0.066 Ang from the COM)
#  exp-6 tail corrections eset and pset       v_e_tail and v_p_tail, folded
#      (main.f, added before prop.dat is          into v_pe_mol_t and v_p_MPa_t
#       written)
#  prop.dat block averages every nblk = 4000  fix ave/time -> prop.txt, same
#      steps (pwat1.dat line 7)                   three columns
#  dipole column of prop.dat = mean           compute dipole/chunk -> v_mu_tot_D
#      magnitude of the TOTAL molecular
#      dipole (permanent + induced)
#
# What cannot be matched (see src/GCPM/gcpm_lammps_vs_fortran.md):
#  - The Fortran integrates with a Gear 4th-order predictor-corrector; LAMMPS
#    uses velocity Verlet.  Trajectories diverge; averages should agree.
#  - The Fortran truncates by molecule COM-COM distance, LAMMPS by atom-atom
#    distance.  This shifts charge-charge (offset H/M sites) at the cutoff
#    shell; dispersion (O ~ at the COM) is unaffected, hence its near-exact
#    match.
#  - The Fortran sums intermolecular Coulomb + explicit reaction-field self
#    terms; the LAMMPS per-pair RF gets the self terms from intramolecular
#    pairs instead.
#  - pair gcpm applies no dispersion tail correction, so pe and press are the
#    untailed values.  The Fortran's analytic eset/pset are reproduced here as
#    equal-style variables and added in the v_pe_mol_t and v_p_MPa_t thermo
#    columns, so those two are the ones to compare with prop.dat.
#  - The initial velocities differ: the Fortran continues from pwatin, this
#    deck draws a Gaussian distribution and lets fix rigid/nvk/small rescale.
#
# Single-frame comparison workflow (energies and forces, no dynamics):
#   1) build the compare-instrumented Fortran (adds dump_compare.f):
#        gfortran -O2 -fno-automatic -ffixed-line-length-132 -w \
#          main.f init.f force.f Pos_alc.f pre_corrc_average.f \
#          diel_cerf_hbond.f dump_compare.f -o md_water_cmp
#   2) run it (needs param, pwat1.dat, pwatin) -> writes frame.dat + eforce.dat
#        ./md_water_cmp
#   3) convert the frame to a LAMMPS data file:
#        python3 pwatin_to_lammps.py frame.dat data.gcpm
#   4) run this input and compare its step-0 thermo line to eforce.dat:
#        evdwl <-> E_disp (exp-6, no tail)   -- matches to ~5 digits
#        pe    <-> E_total (uconf, no tail)  -- offset by the cutoff convention
#                                               and the RF self bookkeeping
# Useful isolations:
#  * dispersion only:        keep as is, compare evdwl to E_disp.
#  * pure smeared Coulomb:   pair_style gcpm 0 0.0 ${rc} ${rc}
#                            and add  'neigh_modify exclude molecule/intra all'
#                            then compare ecoul to E_coul_smear.
#
# Two variants, selecting where the induced dipole lives:
#   COM placement (paper Eq. 3, matches the Fortran):
#     lmp -in in.gcpm  (defaults: data.gcpm5, dipoletype 4)
#   M-site placement (original 4-site decks, ~4.5% weaker dipoles):
#     lmp -in in.gcpm -v datafile data.gcpm -v dipoletype 3
#
# Full-length reference run (982.13 ps, as in pwat1.dat):
#     mpirun -np 8 lmp -in in.gcpm -v nsteps 1000000

variable datafile    index data.gcpm5
variable dipoletype  index 4        # 4 = COM dipole site (data.gcpm5); 3 = M site (data.gcpm)
variable nsteps      index 1000     # Fortran pwat1.dat: 1000000 (982.13 ps)
variable nout        index 200      # Fortran writes ufile/pos.xyz/meansq.dat every 200 steps
variable r           index 1

variable T           index 298.15   # pwat1.dat temperature
variable P           index 1.0      # 1 atm = 0.101 MPa (only used by the npt line below)

variable velseed     index 817324
variable seed        index 576211

# cutoff must equal the Fortran rcut printed at startup (10 sigma capped at
# half the box minus the skin -> 11.220684 Ang for 500 molecules at 0.997 g/cm3)
variable rc          index 11.220684

units real

# skin = 0.3 sigma from pwat1.dat.  The Fortran rebuilds the (molecule COM)
# neighbor list unconditionally every KSORT = 10 steps; LAMMPS rebuilds on the
# usual half-skin displacement check, which is at least as safe.
neighbor 1.107 bin

atom_style hybrid full dipole sphere
WARNING: Atom style hybrid defines both, per-type and per-atom masses; both must be set, but only per-atom masses will be used (src/atom_vec_hybrid.cpp:134)
read_data ${datafile}
read_data data.gcpm5
